# Safety Invariants

These rules are NON-NEGOTIABLE. They override autonomy level and cannot be disabled.

## S4: Cost Ceiling (Always On)

- Maximum session budget: $20
- Before any expensive operation (large file generation, bulk API calls), estimate cost
- If accumulated session cost approaches ceiling: STOP, report, suggest session split
- Log significant operations to `.sdlc/sessions/`

## S5: Checkpoint Discipline (Always On)

- For operations spanning >3 files or >30 minutes: create a checkpoint commit first
- Never leave the repo in an unbuildable state between checkpoints
- If interrupted, work must be resumable from last checkpoint
- Log decision rationale for non-obvious choices

## S6: Ownership Boundaries (Always On)

- Read CODEOWNERS (if exists) before modifying any file
- If file is owned by another team/agent: REFUSE with explanation
- Never modify overlay governance files (.cursor/rules/sdlc/, .copier-answers.sdlc.yml) unless explicitly asked
- Never modify .sdlc/KILLSWITCH (only humans create/remove it)

## Kill Switch

If `.sdlc/KILLSWITCH` file exists → **ALL agent actions are blocked**.
Check for this file at session start and before any write operation.
